# Line endings: LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# Both repos have ALWAYS stored LF -- `git ls-files --eol` reports i/lf for every tracked text
# file, with no exceptions. What differed was the CHECKOUT. Git for Windows ships
# core.autocrlf=true in its *system* config, which neither repo sets and so inherits silently:
# the index stays LF while the files on disk are materialised as CRLF. Anything that then writes
# plain LF -- an editor, a generator, a script doing a string replacement -- leaves one file
# disagreeing with its neighbours. That mixed on-disk state is what kept surfacing as whole-file
# diffs when moving code between the two repositories; the repository itself was never wrong.
#
# `eol=lf` is the fix, because it OVERRIDES core.autocrlf: the working tree is written as LF too,
# so what is on disk matches what is committed, on every machine and for anyone who clones. It
# lives in the repo, so there is no per-machine git config for anyone to remember to set.
#
# LF is not a style preference here. The Makefile's recipes are executed by MSys2 sh, and a stray
# CR at the end of a recipe line is handed to the shell as part of the command.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Build-critical, spelled out so that a future broad exception cannot quietly sweep them up.
Makefile        text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf

# Visual Studio rewrites its own project files with CRLF whenever it saves them. These are
# vestigial here -- IntelliSense only, since MSVC cannot parse devkitA64's libstdc++ -- but
# pinning them stops that rewrite showing up as a diff every time the solution is opened.
*.sln           text eol=crlf
*.vcxproj       text eol=crlf
*.filters       text eol=crlf
*.user          text eol=crlf

# Binaries: never inspected, never converted. Declared explicitly rather than left to Git's
# content heuristic, because a single false positive corrupts the file. The build outputs are
# listed as a guard in case one is ever committed by accident.
*.jpg           binary
*.png           binary
*.ttf           binary
*.nro           binary
*.elf           binary
*.nacp          binary
